# Reproduce Benny’s Screen 06 character comparison

Use a disposable checkout of the isolated source commit in **checks/source.json**. Install the project’s locked dependencies with `npm ci`, build using `npm run build`, then run `npm run test:continuity` and `npm run verify:refs`. The finished albedo, pom, stitch relief and cuff maps ship in **assets/textures/match06**. The implementation uses the retained canonical Benny GLB, fur-shell vertex geometry and game lighting.

For the trial, add **cx06ReferencePink=1** to the retained parameters in **queries.json**. Leave it out for Claudia’s baseline. The previous **cx06LayeredCoat=1** switch remains available as a separate diagnostic. The rolled cuff swatch was recovered from **assets/textures/match06/benny06_cuff.png** on the fitted-knit candidate at commit **393c83ceaed1d3261ce72a3aec2824be18627e03**.

The calibrated hat-fit and pink dye recipe is **tools/benny-reference-pink/fit_reference.py**. Its inputs are the native artwork, the saved canonical actor matrices, the retained native visibility bounds, one previous coat opening, one retained opening and a capture with the retained body hidden. The resulting parameters and measured color quantiles are recorded in **checks/fit.json**. Two original yarn patches are prepared with **tools/benny-reference-pink/bake_yarn.py**. The local height response and fitted garment transform are explicit in **src/characters/benny/referencePink06.ts**.

Run the included capture harness against a loopback Vite server with Playwright 1.57.0, Chromium and FFmpeg. Copy **reproduce** into a writable run directory. Set **RAINBOW_RUN** to this directory, **RAINBOW_BASE_URL** to the server, **RAINBOW_CHROMIUM** to the browser executable and **NODE_PATH** to Playwright and Pixelmatch 7.1.0. Run `node capture.cjs stills 06:BEFORE 06:NEW`, `node capture.cjs ride 06:BEFORE 06:NEW`, and `node capture.cjs full-safe 06:NEW`. **capture-character.cjs** uses the same camera harness to hide individual child meshes in a frozen debug render and measure their visible silhouettes.

The shared fitting inputs **fit-inputs/actor-matrices.json**, **fit-inputs/retained-visible-bounds.json** and **fit-inputs/CLAUDIA_BODY_HIDDEN.png** are supplied here. For the previous material’s source capture use **CODEX_NEW/opening.png** from the earlier layered-coat branch at **35dd903dc09f08d7b3262b9cab2753ad0d40d19c**. The native source texture is already in the inherited working tree.
